 # Offline behavior
 
-Startup behavior is documented by [observation A](../sources/network-a.md).
+## Startup network activity: unresolved
+
+Whether startup makes network calls is **unresolved**. Two observations under the same recorded conditions give conflicting results:
+
+| Observation | Revision and conditions | Command | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| [Observation A](../sources/network-a.md) | synthetic copper-r3, Linux, default config, no external proxy | `capture --window 30 app start` | zero network calls in 30 seconds |
+| [Observation B](../sources/network-b.md) | synthetic copper-r3, Linux, default config, no external proxy | `capture --window 30 app start` | attempted telemetry upload in 30 seconds |
+
+Neither source is dated, and neither records owner acceptance. Their recorded revision, platform, configuration, proxy setting and command are identical, so scope, chronology and authority do not explain the difference. Observation B notes that the discrepancy was not explained. Do not rely on startup making no network calls, or on it always attempting telemetry, until this is resolved.
+
+To resolve it: repeat captures at copper-r3 with the stated command. For each run, record the conditions the sources omit, such as the exact build, user and config state, any prior consent or telemetry setting, network availability, and whether telemetry is sent on first or periodic startup. Then determine which conditions trigger the upload.
